From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] VU1 interpreter: upper executor, hazard check and write bookkeeping inline

What it is for:
  Patch 0018 lets translated VU1 code run the interpreter's per-pair step
  with the pair decoded as a constant. The step still called out of line
  to execUpper (a switch on the opcode, the dest mask in loops),
  calculatePairReadyCycle and markPairWrites (loops over the decoded
  register sets), so the constant pair could not be folded through them.

The change:
  - execUpper and its helpers move unchanged to
    include/runtime/ps2_vu1_upper_inl.h, forced inline, included by
    runtime/ps2_vu1.h (src/lib/vu/ps2_vu1_upper.cpp is left as a stub).
  - In the inline copy the four field extractions (dest, ft, fs, fd) are
    written out: the short helpers of src/lib/vu/ps2_vu1_detail.h would
    clash with ps2xRecomp's FT/FS/FD macros in headers that include both.
  - calculatePairReadyCycle and markPairWrites move unchanged into
    runtime/ps2_vu1.h, forced inline.
  Same results: the code is the same, only where it is compiled changes.
  Tested: ps2xTest 454/454; the Ben 10 port's 40 captured VU1 workloads
  give the same checksums with and without its translated code; its
  translated VU code runs 610 M -> 540 M instructions under callgrind
  (Linux, GCC 13).

